# StencilOverlay

`StencilOverlay` darkens everything outside the stencil. It is an element the size of the stencil with a very large `box-shadow` around it, colored with `currentColor`, so the stencil stays clear while the rest of the image is shaded. It doesn't react to the pointer, so the drag area beneath it still receives events.

Both built-in stencils render it inside their draggable area, around the preview and the grid:

```
DraggableArea
└─ StencilOverlay
   ├─ StencilGrid (optional)
   └─ div.…__preview
```

## Usage

Change the shade by setting the overlay's `color`, through the stencil's `overlayClassName` prop:

```svelte
<Cropper {src} stencilProps={{ overlayClassName: 'light-overlay' }} />

<style>
	:global(.light-overlay) {
		color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
	}
</style>
```

The class is set on an element inside the stencil, so it needs `:global()` (or a global stylesheet). See [Customize Appearance](/docs/guides/customize-appearance#overlay).

In a [custom stencil](/docs/tutorials/custom-stencil), wrap your stencil's content in it:

```svelte
<StencilOverlay class="my-stencil__overlay">
	<div class="my-stencil__preview"></div>
</StencilOverlay>
```

## Props

| Prop       | Type         | Default | Description                                         |
| ---------- | ------------ | ------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
| `class`    | `ClassValue` | —       | Classes for the overlay. Upstream's `className`.    |
| `children` | `Snippet`    | —       | Content drawn inside the stencil area.              |

## CSS classes

| Element | Classes                                                                                                   |
| ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Overlay | `advanced-cropper-stencil-overlay`, plus `advanced-cropper-rectangle-stencil__overlay` (or `circle-stencil`) in the built-in stencils |

The base style sets the shadow and `pointer-events: none`. The default theme sets the color to semi-transparent black. `CircleStencil` rounds the overlay with `border-radius: 50%`, which also rounds its shadow.
